      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: The commit message says: *\"Clear the `.ahb4` region in `system_pre_init()` immediately after enabling the AHB4 clock domain.\"*\n\nNote that `STM32_RCC_AHB4ENR |\u003d BIT(28);` on line 295 enables `BKPRAMEN` (the 4 KB Backup SRAM at `0x38800000`), not D3 SRAM4 (`0x38000000`, where `.ahb4` lives). D3 SRAM4 is controlled by `BIT(29)` (`SRAM4EN`), which is enabled by default out of reset (`RCC_AHB4ENR` reset value is `0x20000000`). Clearing `.ahb4` here in `system_pre_init()` is fine, but please update the commit message so it doesn\u0027t imply `BIT(28)` enables the `.ahb4` SRAM clock.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "c547b871ee795c0df06d16296a1860c9fe5fd15a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0457dd1a_38a76b7f",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 312,
